> gcd x^2*y - y, x*y - y
gcd x^2*y - y, x*y - y
  = y*(x - 1)
    = x*y - y
  check: it divides both exactly, and the cofactors are coprime
  (normalized: integer coefficients without a common factor, leading coefficient positive)
> gcd (x+1)*(y+2), (x+1)*(y+3)
gcd (x + 1)*(y + 2), (x + 1)*(y + 3)
  = x + 1
  check: it divides both exactly, and the cofactors are coprime
  (normalized: integer coefficients without a common factor, leading coefficient positive)
> factor x^2*y^2 - 1
  ucas: factor x^2*y^2 - 1
factor x^2*y^2 - 1
  = x^2*y^2 - 1
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  note: some factors may factor further (several variables, or a degree beyond the search)
> factor x^2 - y^2
  ucas: factor x^2 - y^2
factor x^2 - y^2
  = (x + y)*(x - y)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> expand (x + y)^4
  ucas: expand (x + y)^4
expand (x + y)^4
  = x^4 + 4x^3*y + 6x^2*y^2 + 4x*y^3 + y^4
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> gcd x^2 + x*y, x*y + y^2
gcd x^2 + x*y, x*y + y^2
  = x + y
  check: it divides both exactly, and the cofactors are coprime
  (normalized: integer coefficients without a common factor, leading coefficient positive)
> lcm (x+1)*(y+1), (x+1)*(y+2)
lcm (x + 1)*(y + 1), (x + 1)*(y + 2)
  = (y + 1)*(x + 1)*(y + 2)
    = x*y^2 + 3x*y + 2x + y^2 + 3y + 2
  check: both divide it exactly
> resultant x^2 + y, x - y
resultant x^2 + y, x - y
  in x: y^2 + y
    = y*(y + 1)
